                         Patch Metadata - Gen 2/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_local_search                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace random sampled greedy construction with a deterministic beam search followed by   │
│                          │ makespan-aware local improvement.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The previous code samples only up to ten possible next transactions and commits to one │
│                          │ random starting transaction. This can miss the transaction whose placement produces the   │
│                          │ lowest actual schedule cost.                                                              │
│                          │ 2. The new beam search evaluates every feasible next transaction for several promising    │
│                          │ partial schedules. It uses `workload.get_opt_seq_cost` directly, so selection is based on │
│                          │ the simulator’s true conflict-aware makespan rather than transaction length or write      │
│                          │ counts.                                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. `num_seqs` is now used as the beam width. Keeping multiple prefixes prevents a locally │
│                          │ attractive prefix from permanently excluding a better final ordering.                     │
│                          │ 4. After full schedules are built, insertion local search repeatedly tries relocating     │
│                          │ every transaction to every other position. This repairs ordering mistakes that greedy     │
│                          │ prefix construction cannot undo.                                                          │
│                          │ 5. Objective evaluations are cached because identical schedules can arise during beam     │
│                          │ expansion and local search. This makes the stronger search substantially cheaper than     │
│                          │ repeatedly simulating the same ordering.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned schedule is therefore selected from a broader set of conflict-aware          │
│                          │ candidate orderings and then optimized using direct makespan-reducing moves.              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0322                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
