│ patch_description        │ This redesign replaces random sampled greedy selection with a deterministic search        │
│                          │ pipeline:                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A memoized evaluator avoids recalculating makespans for identical partial or complete  │
│                          │ transaction orders.                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. Small workloads are solved exactly by enumerating all transaction permutations.        │
│                          │ 3. Larger workloads use beam search: at every depth, multiple promising partial schedules │
│                          │ are retained instead of committing to one greedy choice.                                  │
│                          │ 4. The best beam schedules are improved with insertion-based local search, which directly │
│                          │ evaluates makespan changes caused by moving transactions.                                 │
│                          │ 5. Search width is controlled by `num_seqs`, preserving practical runtime while examining │
│                          │ substantially better candidates than the original fixed random sample of ten              │
│                          │ transactions.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improves schedule quality because every chosen transaction is evaluated using the    │
│                          │ real workload makespan rather than transaction length or random selection.                │
