│ patch_name               │ beam_insert_scheduler                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces sampled greedy selection with a cost-aware beam search followed by  │
│                          │ schedule-level local improvement.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key steps:                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Every candidate prefix is evaluated using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, rather than     │
│                          │ transaction length or write counts. This directly optimizes the simulator’s makespan      │
│                          │ model.                                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. A beam keeps several promising partial transaction orders at every depth. Unlike a     │
│                          │ single greedy path, this preserves alternatives when a locally good transaction later     │
│                          │ produces worse conflicts.                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Final beam schedules are refined with best-improving transaction insertion moves.      │
│                          │ Moving a transaction across several conflicting transactions can reduce makespan more     │
│                          │ effectively than only swapping neighboring transactions.                                  │
│                          │ 4. Evaluation results are cached by sequence tuple, avoiding repeated simulator calls     │
│                          │ during beam expansion and local search.                                                   │
│                          │ 5. The beam width and local-search effort are bounded so the approach remains practical   │
│                          │ for larger workloads while using deeper search for smaller workloads.                     │
