├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pair_reinsertion_escape                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Add a conflict-aware two-transaction ejection/reinsertion phase after the existing        │
│                          │ insertion local search.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current local search accepts only one-transaction insertion or exchange moves.     │
│                          │ Such a search can become trapped when two transactions must move together: moving either  │
│                          │ transaction alone temporarily preserves or increases the conflict-induced critical path,  │
│                          │ while moving both produces a lower makespan.                                              │
│                          │ 2. The new phase removes a pair of transactions from the best locally optimized schedule  │
│                          │ and exhaustively tests their reinsertion positions. Every candidate is evaluated through  │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost`, so the decision uses the simulator's true conflict-aware makespan     │
│                          │ rather than operation-count proxies.                                                      │
│                          │ 3. For small and medium instances all source transaction pairs and all destinations are   │
│                          │ examined. Larger instances use evenly distributed source and destination positions,       │
│                          │ preserving long-distance relocation opportunities without making the search prohibitively │
│                          │ expensive.                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Multiple successful rounds allow the optimizer to escape several interacting local     │
│                          │ minima. Only strictly lower makespan schedules are accepted, so this phase cannot degrade │
│                          │ the schedule already found by beam search and single-transaction local search.            │
