╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_neighborhood                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Add an exchange neighborhood to the existing insertion-based local search.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current local search only accepts improving insertion moves. Although insertion    │
│                          │ moves are expressive, a schedule can be a local optimum under every single insertion      │
│                          │ while exchanging two transactions simultaneously reduces conflict-induced waiting.        │
│                          │ 2. Transaction ordering has non-linear conflict effects: moving one transaction alone can │
│                          │ expose another dependency, while swapping two conflicting transactions can resolve both   │
│                          │ delays at once.                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Evaluate pairwise exchanges using the same exact conflict-aware `get_opt_seq_cost`     │
│                          │ objective. This preserves correctness and avoids proxy heuristics.                        │
│                          │ 4. For large workloads, use the same structured position subset already used for          │
│                          │ insertion moves, keeping the added search bounded while still testing long-distance       │
│                          │ exchanges.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This expands the local-search basin explored from each beam solution and can escape       │
│                          │ insertion-only local minima, producing lower makespan schedules.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0179                                                                                   │
