│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_local_search                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Add pairwise-swap best-improvement evaluation to the existing insertion descent.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Insertion moves are effective for relocating a transaction around a conflict chain,    │
│                          │ but they can be trapped when two transactions must exchange positions together.           │
│                          │ 2. A swap directly tests the alternative serialization order of every selected            │
│                          │ transaction pair using `get_opt_seq_cost`, preserving the simulator’s actual makespan as  │
│                          │ the sole objective.                                                                       │
│                          │ 3. The swap search shares the existing evaluation budget, so it remains bounded. It       │
│                          │ evaluates pairs deterministically and only considers an improving schedule.               │
│                          │ 4. This complements insertion search: after identifying the best insertion candidate in a │
│                          │ round, the optimizer can select an even better pairwise exchange before committing the    │
│                          │ next schedule. This is especially useful for read/write conflict patterns where a writer  │
│                          │ and a reader have incompatible effects on several downstream transactions.                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0150                                                                                   │
