│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded contiguous block-relocation neighborhood before swap search.                │
│                          │ Single-transaction insertion can be trapped when two or more transactions must move       │
│                          │ together across the same conflict region: moving either one alone may not reduce the      │
│                          │ critical path, while moving the group preserves their favorable internal ordering and     │
│                          │ removes the inter-group delay. The new search evaluates relocations of blocks of length 2 │
│                          │ through 4 using the same exact conflict-aware `evaluate` objective.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For workloads up to 30 transactions, all valid block starts and reinsertion points are    │
│                          │ examined. For larger workloads, the existing impact- and anchor-selected positions bound  │
│                          │ the neighborhood, preserving the scheduler's scalability while allowing coordinated moves │
│                          │ around measured bottlenecks. Only strict improvements are accepted by the existing        │
│                          │ descent logic, so this cannot return a schedule worse than the prior local-search result. │
