│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_iterated_descent                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded deterministic perturb-and-reoptimize phase after the existing beam-seeded   │
│                          │ local search. The current strict insertion/swap/reversal descent can stop at a local      │
│                          │ optimum even though reaching a better transaction order requires temporarily accepting a  │
│                          │ worse ordering. This edit creates several objectively best non-improving “kicks” from the │
│                          │ best schedule using medium interval reversals, distant exchanges, and short block         │
│                          │ relocations. Each perturbed schedule is then reoptimized with the same conflict-aware     │
│                          │ objective.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Preserve the best schedule obtained from the existing beam and local-search phase.     │
│                          │ 2. Enumerate diverse deterministic perturbations that alter several conflict precedence   │
│                          │ relations at once.                                                                        │
│                          │ 3. Rank perturbations using `get_opt_seq_cost`, retaining only a small bounded number of  │
│                          │ promising kicks.                                                                          │
│                          │ 4. Run strict insertion, exchange, and interval-reversal descent from each kick.          │
│                          │ 5. Keep the globally best makespan found across the original and perturbed local optima.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All decisions continue to use the simulator’s actual makespan rather than                 │
│                          │ transaction-length proxies. The bounded number of kicks limits runtime while allowing the │
│                          │ search to cross local-optimum barriers.                                                   │
