│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ perturbed_local_seeds                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add deterministic perturbation seeds before the existing strict-improvement local search. │
│                          │ The current insertion/swap descent can become trapped when every single improving move is │
│                          │ blocked by an ordering barrier. Reversing a medium interval, relocating a small block,    │
│                          │ and exchanging distant transactions deliberately cross such barriers while preserving a   │
│                          │ valid permutation.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The perturbed schedules are evaluated using the same exact conflict-aware makespan        │
│                          │ objective and are then passed through the existing insertion/swap descent. This combines  │
│                          │ broad deterministic diversification with the current strong local optimizer, without      │
│                          │ relying on transaction-length proxies or random behavior. The original best beam seeds    │
│                          │ are retained, so this extends rather than replaces the existing search.                   │
