│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the conflict-aware beam construction, but strengthens the improvement  │
│                          │ phase with a variable-neighborhood descent and deterministic iterated local search.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Every candidate is evaluated using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so all decisions       │
│                          │ optimize the true transactional makespan.                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Beam search retains multiple promising transaction prefixes instead of committing to   │
│                          │ one greedy order.                                                                         │
│                          │ 3. Local search considers:                                                                │
│                          │    - single transaction insertions,                                                       │
│                          │    - relocation of contiguous blocks of 2–4 transactions,                                 │
│                          │    - arbitrary transaction swaps,                                                         │
│                          │    - exchanges of adjacent transaction blocks.                                            │
│                          │    Block exchanges are useful when multiple transactions must cross a conflict bottleneck │
│                          │ together.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. On large workloads, local search samples both evenly spaced positions and transactions │
│                          │ with the largest measured removal impact. This focuses evaluations on transactions        │
│                          │ actually responsible for makespan.                                                        │
│                          │ 5. After normal descent, deterministic perturbations are applied to the best schedules    │
│                          │ and improved again. This escapes local minima that cannot be improved by one strictly     │
│                          │ improving move.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned schedule remains a valid permutation of all transaction IDs and the output   │
│                          │ interface is unchanged.                                                                   │
