│ patch_name               │ bounded_block_relocation                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a strict-improvement contiguous block-relocation neighborhood to the existing         │
│                          │ insertion, swap, and reversal descent.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A transaction schedule can contain groups of transactions whose internal ordering is      │
│                          │ already beneficial, but whose collective position delays a conflicting group elsewhere.   │
│                          │ Single-transaction insertion breaks such a group apart, while swaps and reversals cannot  │
│                          │ directly move it across the schedule. Relocating blocks of two to four transactions       │
│                          │ preserves useful local ordering while changing multiple conflict edges at once.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For workloads up to 30 transactions, the edit evaluates every block relocation of lengths │
│                          │ 2–4. For larger workloads, it uses the existing objective-driven source and destination   │
│                          │ positions, retaining bounded runtime while concentrating moves around transactions        │
│                          │ identified by actual makespan impact. Every candidate is evaluated through `evaluate`, so │
│                          │ acceptance is based exclusively on the conflict-aware simulator makespan.                 │
