│ patch_name               │ two_stage_diverse_beam                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Use a wider beam during the early half of construction, then reduce it for the later      │
│                          │ depths. Early transaction choices determine many of the eventual read/write dependency    │
│                          │ chains, so retaining more exact-cost prefixes at this stage gives the optimizer more      │
│                          │ structurally distinct complete schedules. The later narrower beam bounds evaluation cost  │
│                          │ once less of the ordering remains undecided.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Keep the existing exact simulator makespan as the sole ranking signal.                 │
│                          │ 2. Increase the early beam capacity up to a bounded multiple of `num_seqs`, while         │
│                          │ applying a workload-size limit to avoid excessive expansion on large inputs.              │
│                          │ 3. Switch to the existing smaller beam capacity around the midpoint, preserving efficient │
│                          │ completion.                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Refine more final beam candidates, since schedules with slightly worse                 │
│                          │ construction-time cost can improve more strongly under insertion/swap local optimization. │
