                        Patch Metadata - Gen 21/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ elite_perturbation_vnd                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Refactor the existing local-search loop into a reusable strict best-improvement           │
│                          │ variable-neighborhood descent (VND), then apply deterministic perturbation-reoptimization │
│                          │ to several distinct elite beam schedules.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. The beam search supplies several good but structurally different complete transaction  │
│                          │ orders.                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Each seed is first optimized using the existing objective-driven insertion, exchange,  │
│                          │ and interval-reversal neighborhoods.                                                      │
│                          │ 3. A single local optimum can be trapped: no one insertion, swap, or reversal improves    │
│                          │ it, while a coordinated multi-transaction displacement could.                             │
│                          │ 4. For the best distinct local optima, generate controlled “kicks” that preserve schedule │
│                          │ validity: interval reversal, block relocation, and distant exchange.                      │
│                          │ 5. Re-run the same strict VND after every kick. A kicked schedule is never accepted       │
│                          │ merely because it is different; it must eventually improve according to                   │
│                          │ `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`.                                                              │
│                          │ 6. This explores multiple attraction basins while retaining deterministic behavior and    │
│                          │ using the true simulator makespan for every decision.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The change is targeted to the local-search stage and keeps exact search for small         │
│                          │ workloads and the conflict-aware beam construction unchanged.                             │
