│ patch_name               │ bounded_ejection_chains                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded two-transaction ejection-chain neighborhood after the existing beam, local  │
│                          │ descent, and kick phases.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Start from the current globally best complete permutation, so the chain search spends  │
│                          │ its budget in the strongest basin found so far.                                           │
│                          │ 2. Estimate removal impact using the actual simulator objective: temporarily remove each  │
│                          │ transaction and measure the makespan reduction. Transactions whose removal reduces        │
│                          │ makespan the most are likely to lie on critical conflict paths.                           │
│                          │ 3. For a small set of high-impact transactions, relocate a first transaction to several   │
│                          │ schedule anchors.                                                                         │
│                          │ 4. From that modified permutation, relocate a second high-impact transaction to another   │
│                          │ anchor. This coordinated pair of relocations can escape optima where neither individual   │
│                          │ insertion is improving.                                                                   │
│                          │ 5. Evaluate every resulting complete permutation directly with `get_opt_seq_cost`, accept │
│                          │ only strict makespan improvements, and run the existing descent only after a promising    │
│                          │ chain is found.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The neighborhood is deliberately bounded by five high-impact transactions and five anchor │
│                          │ positions, keeping the extra simulator calls controlled while allowing coordinated        │
│                          │ changes that insertion, swap, reversal, and the existing single-block kicks cannot        │
│                          │ represent.                                                                                │
