│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ diverse_beam_vnd                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines the current program’s strong variable-neighborhood local            │
│                          │ optimization with the inspiration program’s endpoint-diverse beam retention.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step improvements:                                                                │
│                          │ 1. It retains exact permutation optimization for very small workloads.                    │
│                          │ 2. Beam search evaluates every prefix using the real simulator makespan.                  │
│                          │ 3. Rather than allowing the beam to collapse into nearly identical prefixes, it preserves │
│                          │ the strongest global prefixes while reserving slots for different final transactions.     │
│                          │ This improves exploration of alternative conflict directions.                             │
│                          │ 4. Each leading complete beam schedule is refined using insertion, swap, and              │
│                          │ interval-reversal moves.                                                                  │
│                          │ 5. The best local optima are additionally perturbed through reversals, distant exchanges, │
│                          │ and two-transaction block relocations, then re-optimized. This helps cross local-optimum  │
│                          │ barriers.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 6. All comparisons use `get_opt_seq_cost`; no transaction-length or operation-count proxy │
│                          │ is used.                                                                                  │
