│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_conflict_search                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This version preserves the strongest parts of the current scheduler: exact search for     │
│                          │ small workloads, objective-based beam search, adaptive impact-guided neighborhoods,       │
│                          │ insertion, swap, reversal, and block-relocation local search.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It additionally crossovers the beam-based construction with deterministic greedy          │
│                          │ insertion constructions. Beam search only appends transactions, while greedy insertion    │
│                          │ evaluates every valid insertion point in a partial schedule using the real simulator      │
│                          │ cost. This can construct schedules that append-only beam search cannot reach early        │
│                          │ enough. The resulting insertion-built schedules are added as diverse local-search seeds   │
│                          │ alongside beam and perturbation seeds.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Cache all simulator evaluations by immutable transaction tuple.                        │
│                          │ 2. Solve workloads with at most seven transactions exactly.                               │
│                          │ 3. Build high-quality append-based beam schedules.                                        │
│                          │ 4. Build additional schedules by greedily choosing the transaction and insertion location │
│                          │ with minimum actual partial makespan.                                                     │
│                          │ 5. Perturb leading beam schedules with reversals, block moves, and endpoint exchanges.    │
│                          │ 6. Improve every seed using objective-evaluated insertion, swap, reversal, and short      │
│                          │ block relocation moves.                                                                   │
│                          │ 7. Return the best valid permutation found.                                               │
