│ patch_name               │ adaptive_conflict_local_search                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The existing large-workload local search spends its evaluation budget on the first        │
│                          │ contiguous source positions, so later transactions and swap moves frequently receive no   │
│                          │ consideration. This edit distributes insertion sources across the entire schedule, while  │
│                          │ prioritizing transactions and positions involved in the most recently accepted improving  │
│                          │ move. Successful moves identify conflict-sensitive regions; examining those regions again │
│                          │ is a direct-cost-guided way to continue shortening critical read/write dependency chains. │
│                          │ The search remains deterministic and bounded, but it covers long-distance moves much more │
│                          │ evenly and preserves budget for swap moves.                                               │
